  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the region $R=\\left\\{(x, y) \\in \\mathbb{R} \\times \\mathbb{R}: x \\geq 0\\right.$ and $\\left.y^{2} \\leq 4-x\\right\\}$. Let $\\mathcal{F}$ be the family of all circles that are contained in $R$ and have centers on the $x$-axis. Let $C$ be the circle that has largest radius among the circles in $\\mathcal{F}$. Let $(\\alpha, \\beta)$ be a point where the circle $C$ meets the curve $y^{2}=4-x$.<br>The radius of the circles&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is____.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1.5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/9fcb5f5a-cdeb-4468-9934-738cd9c4dbe8-image.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 191px;\" /></p><p>equation of normal at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Passing through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Also <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>so radius of circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> but in this case circle intersect at three points</p>",
    "image": null
  },
